<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="CreatingObjectRequestsWithInitialVa-CE154BC0" xml:lang="en-us" class="- topic/topic task/task "><title class="- topic/title ">Creating object requests with initial values</title><shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">You can create five objects and configure them with initial
values: Calendar, Event Enrollment, Notification Class, Schedule and
Trend Log.</shortdesc><prolog class="- topic/prolog "><metadata class="- topic/metadata "><keywords class="- topic/keywords "><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">object requests with initial values</indexterm></keywords></metadata></prolog><taskbody class="- topic/body task/taskbody "><prereq class="- topic/section task/prereq ">You are working in <keyword conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/Workbench" class="- topic/keyword "/> connected to your Supervisor station that has been configured
with a BacnetAWSNetwork.</prereq><context class="- topic/section task/context "/><steps class="- topic/ol task/steps "><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">Expand <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Config</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Drivers</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">BacnetAWSNetwork</uicontrol></menucascade>.</cmd><stepresult class="- topic/itemgroup task/stepresult ">The <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">Bacnet Aws Device Manager</wintitle> opens.</stepresult></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">If you have not already done so, click the <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Discover</uicontrol> button.</cmd><stepresult class="- topic/itemgroup task/stepresult ">The driver runs a discovery job to locate all remote controllers
and devices.</stepresult></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">Expand a device and double-click its <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Config</uicontrol> node in the Nav tree.</cmd><stepresult class="- topic/itemgroup task/stepresult ">The <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">Bacnet Aws Config Manager</wintitle> view
displays.</stepresult></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">To create a dynamic object, open the <apiname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/apiname ">bacnet</apiname> palette and drag a BACnet object from the <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Config</uicontrol> folder in palette to the remote controller’s <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Config</uicontrol> folder under the <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">BacnetAWSNetwork</uicontrol>.</cmd><stepresult class="- topic/itemgroup task/stepresult "><note class="- topic/note ">This <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Config</uicontrol> folder
is not the Supervisor station's <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Config</uicontrol> folder.
It is the controller station's <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Config</uicontrol> folder,
which is under the Supervisor station's <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">BACnetAwsNetwork</uicontrol>.</note></stepresult></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">Right–click the object in the <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">Database</wintitle> pane and click <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Views</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Property Sheet</uicontrol></menucascade>.</cmd><stepresult class="- topic/itemgroup task/stepresult ">The object’s <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">Property Sheet</wintitle> opens.</stepresult></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">Enter initial properties and click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Save</uicontrol>.</cmd></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">Right-click the object and click <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Actions</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Create Object</uicontrol></menucascade>.</cmd><stepresult class="- topic/itemgroup task/stepresult ">The driver creates each object, giving each a unique object
identifier and automatically places the object in a <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">dynamicObjects</uicontrol> folder, under the <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">BacnetAwsNetwork</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Local Device</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Export Table</uicontrol></menucascade> in the Supervisor station’s Nav tree.<image placement="break" scale="65" href="../graphic/bacnetDynamicObjFolder_0000065600.png" class="- topic/image "/><note class="- topic/note ">The <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Create Object</uicontrol> action
is not available under a <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">BacnetNetwork</uicontrol>. It
requires the <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">BacnetAwsNetwork</uicontrol>.</note></stepresult></step></steps></taskbody></task>